WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Wittenberg, 1517.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.770
A friar and professor challenges
the preaching of indulgences.

3
00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:10.080
By 1521 he is excommunicated.

4
00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:14.730
He refuses to recant unless convinced
by Scripture and plain reason.

5
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.520
Rome answers with a council
at Trent that meets,

6
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.080
on and off, for 18 years.

7
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:24.110
Four centuries later, bishops from
across the world gather again,

8
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.400
in the Vatican.

9
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:28.630
So in the church, who gets the last word:

10
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.630
the Bible, the Pope, the
bishops, or the people?

11
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.990
In this mission, you'll
compare how Lutheran,

12
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.990
Reformed, Anglican and Anabaptist
churches were organised.

13
00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.490
Then you'll trace how Trent and Vatican
II reshaped authority in the Catholic

14
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.500
Church.

15
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.770
Your mission: find out where
authority in the church really lies.
